# Patient Instructor: "Vigilance" and "When this creature enters, recruit" (CR 701.70a): Bot1 draws the Ornithopter and discards it,
# a nonland card, so a 1/1 white Human Soldier token is created (CR 111.1) under Bot1. Both attack on turn 3: the Instructor has
# vigilance (CR 702.20b) and stays untapped, the token, without it, is tapped.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Patient Instructor
Plains
Plains
Plains
Ornithopter
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Patient Instructor.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Patient Instructor > Bot2; Human Soldier Token > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Patient Instructor.Tapped = false
? Bot1.Battlefield.Human Soldier Token.Tapped = true

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Human Soldier Token.Token = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Human Soldier Token.Colors = White
Bot1.Battlefield.Human Soldier Token.Subtypes = Human; Soldier
Bot1.Battlefield.Human Soldier Token.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Human Soldier Token.Toughness = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Patient Instructor.Keywords = Vigilance
Bot1.Battlefield.Patient Instructor.Power = 2
Bot1.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot2.Life = 17
